{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011s7rA1XUMbCBWb6c5fVLg5","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"c6bdfc9e8020eb1a330145360052e8583055afb8\",\"date\":\"2026-10-15T13:25:14Z\",\"message\":\"(chore) Release v4.6.0\",\"refs\":\"tag: v4.6.0\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"78264205757c39f77e32f5624ae5c62301441bd4\",\"date\":\"2026-10-10T11:58:51-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Switch to using NPM trusted-publication\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"cbef3fb43ccceafd4ddeae3a6ec65516b223eb0b\",\"date\":\"2026-10-08T11:56:26Z\",\"message\":\"(chore) Release v4.5.0\",\"refs\":\"tag: v4.5.0\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"e5adae2d7a1d18ce000d4a3a7587b3f77bcefee8\",\"date\":\"2026-10-07T16:34:27-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#431)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"827b70e647d060eaf53b478c1bebd8987b7a00d9\",\"date\":\"2026-10-07T21:48:50+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Space the report form fields evenly with a Carbon Stack (#423)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Space the report form fields evenly with a Carbon Stack\\n\\nThe run report and edit scheduled report forms now put their fields in\\na Stack with gap={5}, and the form container sets the 16px padding.\\nBefore, each field set its own spacing: fixed heights with\\n30px bottom margins, an extra 50px margin and 32px top padding on the\\noutput format select, and 16px padding on each parameter and the cron\\neditor. That left uneven gaps between the fields.\\n\\nThe Report and Output format selects also lose their fixed 300px width,\\nso every field in both forms is full width like the parameter inputs.\\n\\n* Keep the cron editor's floated fields inside its wrapper\\n\\nThe schedule fields float, so the editor's wrapper only had a height\\nbecause the Stack around it is a grid. display: flow-root makes the\\nwrapper contain them in any parent.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"500361d9aa5a6ce646a3b9aa86796b45842bbcec\",\"date\":\"2026-10-07T18:55:14+05:30\",\"message\":\"(chore) Bump esm-framework peerDependency to 11.x (#429)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi.dilinika@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"c0a92a7950d8e23fe16e914562081f269762077f\",\"date\":\"2026-10-07T15:52:17+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Refresh running report requests and remove dead page routes (#418)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"c727d81885a0c131c4780971a28243de9854998b\",\"date\":\"2026-10-07T15:38:15+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Pin the report overlay's action buttons to the bottom (#419)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The run-report and edit-scheduled-report forms set\\n`justify-content: space-between` on a column that had no height to fill,\\nso the Cancel and Run buttons sat directly under the last input, and the\\ninputs spread apart as the form grew.\\n\\nMake the overlay a flex column, let the form fill it, and push the button\\nset to the bottom with `margin-top: auto` so the inputs stay top-aligned.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"06a5b092b1cd90a40745932a80b20866ab0bec12\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T23:39:28+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Add page headers to the other Reports pages (#414)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Add page headers to the other Reports pages\\n\\nGive the Scheduled reports and Reports data overview pages the same\\nPageHeader and ReportsPictogram as the Reports overview, so all three\\nReports pages share one header.\\n\\nEach page now renders the full-width header followed by its content in\\nthe overview's .content wrapper. This replaces the bare h3 inside a\\n130px white panel that the table and filter form overflowed, and the\\nempty 48px spacer on the Scheduled reports page. The now-unused .page,\\n.mainPanelDiv and .reportsLabelDiv rules are removed.\\n\\nThe Scheduled reports title's default text drops the \\\"Scheduld\\\" typo.\\nThe data overview test mocks the header and checks that it renders.\\n\\n* Test the Scheduled reports page header\\n\\nThe Scheduled reports page had no test, so nothing checked its new header. Add one that renders the page and checks for the heading, the pictogram and a scheduled report row.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"0e8bbe0a4b6401d45f0c7da3f26b2d3848508ef1\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T16:33:05-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#415)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"e497c33d0dc9799605b6ab663ddb54f967d8a682\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T22:50:33+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Add a page header with the reports pictogram to Reports (#408)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) Add a page header with the reports pictogram to Reports\\n\\nReplaces the bare \\\"Reports\\\" heading on the overview page with\\nPageHeader and PageHeaderContent, using the styleguide's new\\nReportsPictogram. The header runs full width under the navbar, with the\\nimplementation name above the title like other O3 apps, a white\\nbackground, a bottom border, and 16px of space before the action\\nbuttons.\\n\\nThe root container's 32px padding moves onto each page's content so\\nthe header can sit flush. The overview no longer passes the\\nbreadcrumb slot's negative top margin, which only offset that padding\\nand would otherwise pull the header under the navbar. The scheduled\\nreports and Reports Webview pages keep the same padding through a page\\nwrapper, so their layout doesn't change.\\n\\nReportsPictogram ships in a framework release after\\nopenmrs/openmrs-esm-core adds it, so this needs that release before it\\ntypechecks.\\n\\n* Mock the page header in the overview tests\\n\\nThe overview tests mock @openmrs/esm-framework with a factory that only\\nlists the exports they use. The overview now renders PageHeader,\\nPageHeaderContent and ReportsPictogram, so add simple mocks for them.\\n\\n* Assert that the Reports overview renders its page header\\n\\nThe overview test mocked PageHeader, PageHeaderContent and\\nReportsPictogram but never checked them, so it would still pass if the\\nheader or pictogram were removed. It now checks for the \\\"Reports\\\"\\nheading and the pictogram.\\n\\n* Drop the breadcrumbs slot from the Reports overview\\n\\nNothing renders into breadcrumbs-slot any more. No extension attaches to\\nit, and the app shell no longer mounts its breadcrumbs component. The\\noverview's slot had no class, so it rendered as an empty element and\\nremoving it doesn't change the layout. The test mock for ExtensionSlot\\ngoes with it.\\n\\n* Rename tests to drop the .component suffix\\n\\nTest files don't carry the component-kind suffix. Rename the three that\\ndid in admin-tools:\\n\\n- reports-app overview.component.test.tsx -> overview.test.tsx\\n- reports-app reports-data-overview.component.test.tsx -> reports-data-overview.test.tsx\\n- metadataexport-app view-package-action-button.component.test.tsx -> view-package-action-button.test.tsx\\n\\nThe only content change is the trailing newline Prettier adds to\\nreports-data-overview.test.tsx.\\n\\n* Remove breadcrumbs from the Reports app\\n\\nNothing renders into breadcrumbs-slot any more, so the Reports pages\\nwere rendering empty slots and registering breadcrumbs nobody reads.\\n\\n- Remove the breadcrumbs slot from the Scheduled reports and Reports\\n  data overview pages, and the .breadcrumb rule. Its negative top margin\\n  cancelled the page's top padding, so .page now drops its top padding\\n  instead and the content stays flush under the navbar.\\n- Remove the registerBreadcrumbs call from startupApp, along with the\\n  getFixedT setup that only it used.\\n- Drop the ExtensionSlot mock from the data overview test.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"f462a28bf6f97d3a1c963e362b79c31b56f69bd4\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T22:25:19+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5993: Reports app shows literal {parameters} instead of the missing parameter names (#376)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* O3-5993: Reports app shows literal {parameters} instead of the missing parameter names\\n\\n* Revert non-English translation changes\\n\\nRestore every translation file except en.json to its state on main.\\nOnly en.json is maintained in this repo; the other locales are managed\\nin Transifex and synced back by the tx-pull workflow, so they'll pick up\\nthe {{parameters}} placeholder from there.\",\"authorName\":\"jwnasambu\",\"authorEmail\":\"33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"feb0ba00e3382e0c55e4b3615648217d7d619198\",\"date\":\"2026-10-01T22:20:05+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Remove unused stylesheet classes from the reports app\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Delete 13 CSS Module classes in esm-reports-app that no component\\nreferences. Each stylesheet is a CSS Module, so a class only applies\\nwhen a file that imports that stylesheet uses it as styles.<name>, and\\nnone of these are:\\n\\n- root.scss: welcome, explainer (plus the @carbon/type import, which\\n  only welcome used)\\n- components/reports.scss: emptyButton, breadcrumbsSlot\\n- components/overlay.scss: closeButton, overlayContent (the desktop and\\n  tablet breakpoint blocks contained only overlayContent)\\n- components/run-report/run-report-form.scss: parameterElement,\\n  cancelActionButton, tableIcon, rowCellEven, rowCellOdd\\n- components/edit-scheduled-report/edit-scheduled-report-form.scss:\\n  reportButton\\n- components/simple-cron-editor/simple-cron-editor.scss: cronEditor\\n\\nrowCellEven, rowCellOdd and reportButton are still in use, but from\\nother stylesheets: the overview tables use the copies in reports.scss,\\nand the run report form uses the copy in run-report-form.scss. Only the\\nunreferenced duplicates are removed.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"fbda030326a3a0a691844ad052fe7aed34ca44ac\",\"date\":\"2026-10-01T21:08:13+03:00\",\"message\":\"chore: Remove inert Carbon CSS rules from reports app (#358)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"solomonfortune\",\"authorEmail\":\"solomonbuwule@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"e7b618c8853787677ac28a20580d588eb2b1c6c0\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29T01:55:37+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Declare react-dom as a peer dependency (#391)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Add react-dom 18.x to peerDependencies in the metadata export and reports apps.\\n\\nThe app shell provides react-dom through module federation, but the\\nOpenMRS rspack config only shares the dependencies an app lists in\\npeerDependencies. Without react-dom listed there, the app loads the\\ncopy of react-dom bundled into its own build instead of the shell's.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"3b89049a21f459607357c7704b11137465d948a1\",\"date\":\"2026-09-27T00:43:49+05:30\",\"message\":\"(chore) O3-5860: Add @carbon/react to peerDependencies (#324)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Declare @carbon/react as a 1.x peer in the OCL, patient documents admin, reports, system admin and metadata export apps, so the build tooling shares it with the app shell instead of bundling a separate copy.\",\"authorName\":\"Pankhudi_Singh\",\"authorEmail\":\"pankhudisingh121206@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"a79ac9c27842f7ada09334751547e76c49ca4022\",\"date\":\"2026-09-25T14:31:04-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Remove reliance on openmrsObservableFetch (#380)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"94c7abeb991c9544f034a6dc732ad4020a07566d\",\"date\":\"2026-09-21T22:23:40+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) O3-5924: Remove unused image annotation dependency (#371)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Remove react-image-annotate from the reports app. The dependency was added with the reports dashboard but has no source or configuration references.\\n\\nRegenerate the lockfile to remove its unused dependency tree without upgrading retained packages. Keep the ref initialisation change separate.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"c57716bd1b210b880f9ad7b096569454b3783048\",\"date\":\"2026-09-21T18:21:18+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Share SWR through module federation in the reports app (#372)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (chore) Share SWR through module federation in the reports app\\n\\nAdd swr to the reports app's peerDependencies so the build tooling\\nfederates it, and pin the exact 2.5.1 dependency the way the other\\npackages in this repo do so the fallback copy matches the app shell.\\n\\nThe openmrs rspack config derives the module federation shared list\\nfrom peerDependencies. swr was only reaching the reports app\\ntransitively, so the built entry registered no swr share and bundled a\\nprivate copy. useSWR from that copy reads its own SWRConfig context,\\nnot the one the framework's component decorator provides, so the\\nreports app ran with SWR's stock defaults (revalidate on focus and\\nreconnect, unlimited retries on every error) and its own cache instead\\nof the shared one. The other four packages here already declare the\\npeer.\\n\\nWith the peer declared, the built entry registers swr, swr/_internal,\\nswr/immutable and swr/infinite at 2.5.1, matching the other O3 apps.\\n\\n* Invalidate report lists through the SWR config's mutate\\n\\nThe cancel modal refreshed the report tables with the global mutate\\nimported from swr. That function is bound to SWR's default cache, while\\nevery hook rendered under the framework's component decorator lives in\\nthe decorator's provider cache, so once swr is federated the global\\nmutate no longer reaches those hooks and the tables would not refresh\\nafter a cancel or delete. Take mutate from useSWRConfig instead, which\\nis bound to the provider cache, and wrap the helper in useCallback so\\nthe submit handler's dependency list stays honest.\\n\\n---------\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"d7d9d35216cc9518ad3835bc5708700bbfe71895\",\"date\":\"2026-09-20T22:23:24+03:00\",\"message\":\"(docs) Fix README CI badges\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Point the OCL, reports and system administration badges to the admin-\\ntools CI workflow instead of the template app workflow.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"denniskigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"e4a4e7e0cc4ec009e2ac7530e0bacacafce1e5df\",\"date\":\"2026-09-15T01:06:36+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Use framework modal for report exports (#352)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Register the report column picker with the framework modal system. Keep column selections in the report viewer so cancelling and reopening preserves them, and include modal files in translation extraction.\\n\\nAdd coverage for selection changes, cancellation, and export.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"dc3c133a5e048e878e0bb6ef063109f7c0dfc345\",\"date\":\"2026-08-29T01:17:06+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Clean build outputs before bundle size comparison (#341)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"bcbb3ed02474f3478554625b4bc1d689c57067c9\",\"date\":\"2026-08-12T11:06:55+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Adopt @openmrs/eslint-config and ESLint 9 (#325)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (chore) Adopt @openmrs/eslint-config and ESLint 9\\n\\nReplace the legacy ESLint setup with the shared flat config and update workspace scripts and dependencies for ESLint 9.\\n\\nPreserve the repository-specific hook rules, track the flat config in Turbo, and fix assertions exposed by the updated lint rules.\\n\\n* Keep ESLint config out of next updates\\n\\nReplace the @openmrs wildcard with the packages this repository actually tracks on the next tag. This prevents the stable-only ESLint config from breaking the scheduled dependency update workflow.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"a0a66e95b1ebba722b9d7d80b61693cca7499518\",\"date\":\"2026-07-09T16:56:25-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#306)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"e7e0cad4e894e064e61bef6ae9ab0296ab0ff545\",\"date\":\"2026-07-06T16:57:59-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#305)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"26a79a0c6d56c8f4951bacbb5e6a16f39947eb73\",\"date\":\"2026-06-10T07:49:09-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Release v4.4.0 (#296)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* chore(release): v4.4.0\\n\\n* Downgrade version from 4.4.0 to 4.3.1\\n\\n* Downgrade version from 4.4.0 to 4.3.1\\n\\n* Downgrade version from 4.4.0 to 4.3.1\\n\\n* Update package.json\\n\\n* Update package.json\\n\\n* Update package.json\\n\\n* Update package.json\\n\\n* Update package.json\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Wikum Weerakutti <wikum@linuxdeveloper.space>\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"81ca025f928ad333b25aa5ae42c88eb166cef5c7\",\"date\":\"2026-06-09T17:33:12+05:30\",\"message\":\"(chore) Bump @openmrs/esm-framework peer dependency to 10.x (#295)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi.dilinika@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"6f75b4ca50fce3308d0e1530adb56cce7c087a13\",\"date\":\"2026-05-14T21:52:41+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Migrate from jest to vitest (#277)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"6a0bca24a514292c45b94dda2a653f0aa434e83f\",\"date\":\"2026-04-06T17:00:19-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#256)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"0c1fa25ea77d35b0c36f5650427c33b319f3c76e\",\"date\":\"2026-03-31T10:07:50-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#248)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"85ce3c1b0bc9e64f21b122fffe22487425801ba7\",\"date\":\"2026-03-31T09:58:23-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#247)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies\\n\\n* (chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies\\n\\nAlso switches to rspack\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Ian <ian.c.bacher@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"a58745170b39fe31f39b2a76b89ca46ad48c30a2\",\"date\":\"2026-02-19T21:50:59+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Release v4.3.0 (#238)\",\"refs\":\"tag: v4.3.0\",\"body\":\"- Bump version to 4.3.0\\n- Bump esm-framework peer dependency to 9.x across all packages\\n- Pin webpack to 5.99.9 to fix potential build failures\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"d631bae67f92ce1625be3b2c70020b410d101c63\",\"date\":\"2026-02-10T11:05:41-05:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"f9421aa8ed46a3ab5e9ec59c832ba66394d83b10\",\"date\":\"2026-01-13T15:45:03-05:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#225)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"026f56a62a963640a3816e79adc018f906692a82\",\"date\":\"2025-12-08T15:39:39-05:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#210)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"a10120fa4fe525b60a32af2b713bccf0377bf2ad\",\"date\":\"2025-12-08T13:37:43+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Add ability to configure web preview url for reports (#190)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"CynthiaKamau\",\"authorEmail\":\"cynthiakamau54@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"ced1f937c37c3631813b8ebcc4a39ce3dd74a917\",\"date\":\"2025-12-08T10:38:07+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Add ability to configure fetching reports without all parameters (#185)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"CynthiaKamau\",\"authorEmail\":\"cynthiakamau54@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"0d2f9245d876ed97b23a934c903581c1c15c3012\",\"date\":\"2025-11-19T15:35:05-05:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#196)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"c6a961a02fe7ae143e49c13bb82da6df03c17c96\",\"date\":\"2025-11-14T15:38:36-05:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#195)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"1d0cf49744cec33e70b00927ac6c33c7858eb83b\",\"date\":\"2025-11-12T15:37:49-05:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#193)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"c9af3cb4ffbfac7924dc849e83dee22e11e7b972\",\"date\":\"2025-11-12T12:19:29+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Add support for concepts in report parameters (#184)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"CynthiaKamau\",\"authorEmail\":\"cynthiakamau54@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"cb823c54259513f9b1bbd61225f89708de9312c7\",\"date\":\"2025-10-20T21:22:02+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Expand webservices.rest dependency range to support 3.x\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Updates webservices.rest backend dependency version constraint from ^2.2.0 (or ^2.24.0) to \\\">=2.2.0\\\" to support both 2.x stable releases and 3.x pre-release/stable versions. This resolves version compatibility issues when running with webservices.rest 3.0.0-SNAPSHOT.0.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2425e09469bfc376cd5bde7d56da8f24bffc7686\",\"date\":\"2025-10-17T21:47:37+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Upgrade i18next ecosystem to v25/v16/v9.3\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"- Update i18next from ^21.10.0 to ^25.0.0\\n- Update react-i18next from ^11.18.6 to ^16.0.0\\n- Update i18next-parser from ^6.6.0 to ^9.3.0\\n- Update TypeScript from ^4.0.3 to ^5.0.0 (required for i18next v25)\\n- Align with core repository i18next upgrade (PR #1473)\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"13b72b3c975bb98b7c4791e89783a95cf43e6549\",\"date\":\"2025-09-08T16:35:24-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#159)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"7f31bb52217a47134f01519570f2349bc9bfdcd1\",\"date\":\"2025-08-13T16:38:13-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#147)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"0ecb9b39fd2df03af600e4d44a3c84d1ef51bbf4\",\"date\":\"2025-08-08T16:38:41-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#146)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"b2fc17c1b3b7cb4b6e69582727e15c64bf7af316\",\"date\":\"2025-08-08T11:26:03+05:30\",\"message\":\"(chore) Release v4.2.0\",\"refs\":\"tag: v4.2.0\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"jayasanka-sack\",\"authorEmail\":\"33048395+jayasanka-sack@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"7428eb74419d8acf3d42b77bf71604e1c60993f8\",\"date\":\"2025-06-26T16:38:53-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#120)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"f4121716f2eddffbe765711c20f017e165d00f0d\",\"date\":\"2025-06-03T16:37:34-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#101)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"9795d776cd61b56114d4da597e9b0be1abbe5ff5\",\"date\":\"2025-06-03T13:37:50-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Fix the auto-update script and update to the latest version of core (#99)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"}],\"totalCount\":72}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"18005517-9fe5-4943-8b94-df897eb41584","uuid":"607b8d0d-7fe2-407c-902e-98e2925c5da9","timestamp":"2026-10-23T15:07:17.607Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"c6bdfc9e8020eb1a330145360052e8583055afb8\",\"date\":\"2026-10-15T13:25:14Z\",\"message\":\"(chore) Release v4.6.0\",\"refs\":\"tag: v4.6.0\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"78264205757c39f77e32f5624ae5c62301441bd4\",\"date\":\"2026-10-10T11:58:51-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Switch to using NPM trusted-publication\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"cbef3fb43ccceafd4ddeae3a6ec65516b223eb0b\",\"date\":\"2026-10-08T11:56:26Z\",\"message\":\"(chore) Release v4.5.0\",\"refs\":\"tag: v4.5.0\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"e5adae2d7a1d18ce000d4a3a7587b3f77bcefee8\",\"date\":\"2026-10-07T16:34:27-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#431)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"827b70e647d060eaf53b478c1bebd8987b7a00d9\",\"date\":\"2026-10-07T21:48:50+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Space the report form fields evenly with a Carbon Stack (#423)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Space the report form fields evenly with a Carbon Stack\\n\\nThe run report and edit scheduled report forms now put their fields in\\na Stack with gap={5}, and the form container sets the 16px padding.\\nBefore, each field set its own spacing: fixed heights with\\n30px bottom margins, an extra 50px margin and 32px top padding on the\\noutput format select, and 16px padding on each parameter and the cron\\neditor. That left uneven gaps between the fields.\\n\\nThe Report and Output format selects also lose their fixed 300px width,\\nso every field in both forms is full width like the parameter inputs.\\n\\n* Keep the cron editor's floated fields inside its wrapper\\n\\nThe schedule fields float, so the editor's wrapper only had a height\\nbecause the Stack around it is a grid. display: flow-root makes the\\nwrapper contain them in any parent.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"500361d9aa5a6ce646a3b9aa86796b45842bbcec\",\"date\":\"2026-10-07T18:55:14+05:30\",\"message\":\"(chore) Bump esm-framework peerDependency to 11.x (#429)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi.dilinika@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"c0a92a7950d8e23fe16e914562081f269762077f\",\"date\":\"2026-10-07T15:52:17+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Refresh running report requests and remove dead page routes (#418)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"c727d81885a0c131c4780971a28243de9854998b\",\"date\":\"2026-10-07T15:38:15+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Pin the report overlay's action buttons to the bottom (#419)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The run-report and edit-scheduled-report forms set\\n`justify-content: space-between` on a column that had no height to fill,\\nso the Cancel and Run buttons sat directly under the last input, and the\\ninputs spread apart as the form grew.\\n\\nMake the overlay a flex column, let the form fill it, and push the button\\nset to the bottom with `margin-top: auto` so the inputs stay top-aligned.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"06a5b092b1cd90a40745932a80b20866ab0bec12\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T23:39:28+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Add page headers to the other Reports pages (#414)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Add page headers to the other Reports pages\\n\\nGive the Scheduled reports and Reports data overview pages the same\\nPageHeader and ReportsPictogram as the Reports overview, so all three\\nReports pages share one header.\\n\\nEach page now renders the full-width header followed by its content in\\nthe overview's .content wrapper. This replaces the bare h3 inside a\\n130px white panel that the table and filter form overflowed, and the\\nempty 48px spacer on the Scheduled reports page. The now-unused .page,\\n.mainPanelDiv and .reportsLabelDiv rules are removed.\\n\\nThe Scheduled reports title's default text drops the \\\"Scheduld\\\" typo.\\nThe data overview test mocks the header and checks that it renders.\\n\\n* Test the Scheduled reports page header\\n\\nThe Scheduled reports page had no test, so nothing checked its new header. Add one that renders the page and checks for the heading, the pictogram and a scheduled report row.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"0e8bbe0a4b6401d45f0c7da3f26b2d3848508ef1\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T16:33:05-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#415)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"e497c33d0dc9799605b6ab663ddb54f967d8a682\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T22:50:33+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Add a page header with the reports pictogram to Reports (#408)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) Add a page header with the reports pictogram to Reports\\n\\nReplaces the bare \\\"Reports\\\" heading on the overview page with\\nPageHeader and PageHeaderContent, using the styleguide's new\\nReportsPictogram. The header runs full width under the navbar, with the\\nimplementation name above the title like other O3 apps, a white\\nbackground, a bottom border, and 16px of space before the action\\nbuttons.\\n\\nThe root container's 32px padding moves onto each page's content so\\nthe header can sit flush. The overview no longer passes the\\nbreadcrumb slot's negative top margin, which only offset that padding\\nand would otherwise pull the header under the navbar. The scheduled\\nreports and Reports Webview pages keep the same padding through a page\\nwrapper, so their layout doesn't change.\\n\\nReportsPictogram ships in a framework release after\\nopenmrs/openmrs-esm-core adds it, so this needs that release before it\\ntypechecks.\\n\\n* Mock the page header in the overview tests\\n\\nThe overview tests mock @openmrs/esm-framework with a factory that only\\nlists the exports they use. The overview now renders PageHeader,\\nPageHeaderContent and ReportsPictogram, so add simple mocks for them.\\n\\n* Assert that the Reports overview renders its page header\\n\\nThe overview test mocked PageHeader, PageHeaderContent and\\nReportsPictogram but never checked them, so it would still pass if the\\nheader or pictogram were removed. It now checks for the \\\"Reports\\\"\\nheading and the pictogram.\\n\\n* Drop the breadcrumbs slot from the Reports overview\\n\\nNothing renders into breadcrumbs-slot any more. No extension attaches to\\nit, and the app shell no longer mounts its breadcrumbs component. The\\noverview's slot had no class, so it rendered as an empty element and\\nremoving it doesn't change the layout. The test mock for ExtensionSlot\\ngoes with it.\\n\\n* Rename tests to drop the .component suffix\\n\\nTest files don't carry the component-kind suffix. Rename the three that\\ndid in admin-tools:\\n\\n- reports-app overview.component.test.tsx -> overview.test.tsx\\n- reports-app reports-data-overview.component.test.tsx -> reports-data-overview.test.tsx\\n- metadataexport-app view-package-action-button.component.test.tsx -> view-package-action-button.test.tsx\\n\\nThe only content change is the trailing newline Prettier adds to\\nreports-data-overview.test.tsx.\\n\\n* Remove breadcrumbs from the Reports app\\n\\nNothing renders into breadcrumbs-slot any more, so the Reports pages\\nwere rendering empty slots and registering breadcrumbs nobody reads.\\n\\n- Remove the breadcrumbs slot from the Scheduled reports and Reports\\n  data overview pages, and the .breadcrumb rule. Its negative top margin\\n  cancelled the page's top padding, so .page now drops its top padding\\n  instead and the content stays flush under the navbar.\\n- Remove the registerBreadcrumbs call from startupApp, along with the\\n  getFixedT setup that only it used.\\n- Drop the ExtensionSlot mock from the data overview test.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"f462a28bf6f97d3a1c963e362b79c31b56f69bd4\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T22:25:19+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5993: Reports app shows literal {parameters} instead of the missing parameter names (#376)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* O3-5993: Reports app shows literal {parameters} instead of the missing parameter names\\n\\n* Revert non-English translation changes\\n\\nRestore every translation file except en.json to its state on main.\\nOnly en.json is maintained in this repo; the other locales are managed\\nin Transifex and synced back by the tx-pull workflow, so they'll pick up\\nthe {{parameters}} placeholder from there.\",\"authorName\":\"jwnasambu\",\"authorEmail\":\"33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"feb0ba00e3382e0c55e4b3615648217d7d619198\",\"date\":\"2026-10-01T22:20:05+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Remove unused stylesheet classes from the reports app\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Delete 13 CSS Module classes in esm-reports-app that no component\\nreferences. Each stylesheet is a CSS Module, so a class only applies\\nwhen a file that imports that stylesheet uses it as styles.<name>, and\\nnone of these are:\\n\\n- root.scss: welcome, explainer (plus the @carbon/type import, which\\n  only welcome used)\\n- components/reports.scss: emptyButton, breadcrumbsSlot\\n- components/overlay.scss: closeButton, overlayContent (the desktop and\\n  tablet breakpoint blocks contained only overlayContent)\\n- components/run-report/run-report-form.scss: parameterElement,\\n  cancelActionButton, tableIcon, rowCellEven, rowCellOdd\\n- components/edit-scheduled-report/edit-scheduled-report-form.scss:\\n  reportButton\\n- components/simple-cron-editor/simple-cron-editor.scss: cronEditor\\n\\nrowCellEven, rowCellOdd and reportButton are still in use, but from\\nother stylesheets: the overview tables use the copies in reports.scss,\\nand the run report form uses the copy in run-report-form.scss. Only the\\nunreferenced duplicates are removed.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"fbda030326a3a0a691844ad052fe7aed34ca44ac\",\"date\":\"2026-10-01T21:08:13+03:00\",\"message\":\"chore: Remove inert Carbon CSS rules from reports app (#358)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"solomonfortune\",\"authorEmail\":\"solomonbuwule@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"e7b618c8853787677ac28a20580d588eb2b1c6c0\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29T01:55:37+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Declare react-dom as a peer dependency (#391)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Add react-dom 18.x to peerDependencies in the metadata export and reports apps.\\n\\nThe app shell provides react-dom through module federation, but the\\nOpenMRS rspack config only shares the dependencies an app lists in\\npeerDependencies. Without react-dom listed there, the app loads the\\ncopy of react-dom bundled into its own build instead of the shell's.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"3b89049a21f459607357c7704b11137465d948a1\",\"date\":\"2026-09-27T00:43:49+05:30\",\"message\":\"(chore) O3-5860: Add @carbon/react to peerDependencies (#324)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Declare @carbon/react as a 1.x peer in the OCL, patient documents admin, reports, system admin and metadata export apps, so the build tooling shares it with the app shell instead of bundling a separate copy.\",\"authorName\":\"Pankhudi_Singh\",\"authorEmail\":\"pankhudisingh121206@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"a79ac9c27842f7ada09334751547e76c49ca4022\",\"date\":\"2026-09-25T14:31:04-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Remove reliance on openmrsObservableFetch (#380)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"94c7abeb991c9544f034a6dc732ad4020a07566d\",\"date\":\"2026-09-21T22:23:40+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) O3-5924: Remove unused image annotation dependency (#371)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Remove react-image-annotate from the reports app. The dependency was added with the reports dashboard but has no source or configuration references.\\n\\nRegenerate the lockfile to remove its unused dependency tree without upgrading retained packages. Keep the ref initialisation change separate.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"c57716bd1b210b880f9ad7b096569454b3783048\",\"date\":\"2026-09-21T18:21:18+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Share SWR through module federation in the reports app (#372)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (chore) Share SWR through module federation in the reports app\\n\\nAdd swr to the reports app's peerDependencies so the build tooling\\nfederates it, and pin the exact 2.5.1 dependency the way the other\\npackages in this repo do so the fallback copy matches the app shell.\\n\\nThe openmrs rspack config derives the module federation shared list\\nfrom peerDependencies. swr was only reaching the reports app\\ntransitively, so the built entry registered no swr share and bundled a\\nprivate copy. useSWR from that copy reads its own SWRConfig context,\\nnot the one the framework's component decorator provides, so the\\nreports app ran with SWR's stock defaults (revalidate on focus and\\nreconnect, unlimited retries on every error) and its own cache instead\\nof the shared one. The other four packages here already declare the\\npeer.\\n\\nWith the peer declared, the built entry registers swr, swr/_internal,\\nswr/immutable and swr/infinite at 2.5.1, matching the other O3 apps.\\n\\n* Invalidate report lists through the SWR config's mutate\\n\\nThe cancel modal refreshed the report tables with the global mutate\\nimported from swr. That function is bound to SWR's default cache, while\\nevery hook rendered under the framework's component decorator lives in\\nthe decorator's provider cache, so once swr is federated the global\\nmutate no longer reaches those hooks and the tables would not refresh\\nafter a cancel or delete. Take mutate from useSWRConfig instead, which\\nis bound to the provider cache, and wrap the helper in useCallback so\\nthe submit handler's dependency list stays honest.\\n\\n---------\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"d7d9d35216cc9518ad3835bc5708700bbfe71895\",\"date\":\"2026-09-20T22:23:24+03:00\",\"message\":\"(docs) Fix README CI badges\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Point the OCL, reports and system administration badges to the admin-\\ntools CI workflow instead of the template app workflow.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"denniskigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"e4a4e7e0cc4ec009e2ac7530e0bacacafce1e5df\",\"date\":\"2026-09-15T01:06:36+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Use framework modal for report exports (#352)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Register the report column picker with the framework modal system. Keep column selections in the report viewer so cancelling and reopening preserves them, and include modal files in translation extraction.\\n\\nAdd coverage for selection changes, cancellation, and export.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"dc3c133a5e048e878e0bb6ef063109f7c0dfc345\",\"date\":\"2026-08-29T01:17:06+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Clean build outputs before bundle size comparison (#341)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"bcbb3ed02474f3478554625b4bc1d689c57067c9\",\"date\":\"2026-08-12T11:06:55+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Adopt @openmrs/eslint-config and ESLint 9 (#325)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (chore) Adopt @openmrs/eslint-config and ESLint 9\\n\\nReplace the legacy ESLint setup with the shared flat config and update workspace scripts and dependencies for ESLint 9.\\n\\nPreserve the repository-specific hook rules, track the flat config in Turbo, and fix assertions exposed by the updated lint rules.\\n\\n* Keep ESLint config out of next updates\\n\\nReplace the @openmrs wildcard with the packages this repository actually tracks on the next tag. This prevents the stable-only ESLint config from breaking the scheduled dependency update workflow.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"a0a66e95b1ebba722b9d7d80b61693cca7499518\",\"date\":\"2026-07-09T16:56:25-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#306)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"e7e0cad4e894e064e61bef6ae9ab0296ab0ff545\",\"date\":\"2026-07-06T16:57:59-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#305)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"26a79a0c6d56c8f4951bacbb5e6a16f39947eb73\",\"date\":\"2026-06-10T07:49:09-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Release v4.4.0 (#296)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* chore(release): v4.4.0\\n\\n* Downgrade version from 4.4.0 to 4.3.1\\n\\n* Downgrade version from 4.4.0 to 4.3.1\\n\\n* Downgrade version from 4.4.0 to 4.3.1\\n\\n* Update package.json\\n\\n* Update package.json\\n\\n* Update package.json\\n\\n* Update package.json\\n\\n* Update package.json\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Wikum Weerakutti <wikum@linuxdeveloper.space>\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"81ca025f928ad333b25aa5ae42c88eb166cef5c7\",\"date\":\"2026-06-09T17:33:12+05:30\",\"message\":\"(chore) Bump @openmrs/esm-framework peer dependency to 10.x (#295)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi.dilinika@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"6f75b4ca50fce3308d0e1530adb56cce7c087a13\",\"date\":\"2026-05-14T21:52:41+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Migrate from jest to vitest (#277)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"6a0bca24a514292c45b94dda2a653f0aa434e83f\",\"date\":\"2026-04-06T17:00:19-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#256)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infras