{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BkCoS26d9454AjMuu2VSGB","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"06a5b092b1cd90a40745932a80b20866ab0bec12\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T23:39:28+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Add page headers to the other Reports pages (#414)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Add page headers to the other Reports pages\\n\\nGive the Scheduled reports and Reports data overview pages the same\\nPageHeader and ReportsPictogram as the Reports overview, so all three\\nReports pages share one header.\\n\\nEach page now renders the full-width header followed by its content in\\nthe overview's .content wrapper. This replaces the bare h3 inside a\\n130px white panel that the table and filter form overflowed, and the\\nempty 48px spacer on the Scheduled reports page. The now-unused .page,\\n.mainPanelDiv and .reportsLabelDiv rules are removed.\\n\\nThe Scheduled reports title's default text drops the \\\"Scheduld\\\" typo.\\nThe data overview test mocks the header and checks that it renders.\\n\\n* Test the Scheduled reports page header\\n\\nThe Scheduled reports page had no test, so nothing checked its new header. Add one that renders the page and checks for the heading, the pictogram and a scheduled report row.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"e497c33d0dc9799605b6ab663ddb54f967d8a682\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T22:50:33+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Add a page header with the reports pictogram to Reports (#408)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) Add a page header with the reports pictogram to Reports\\n\\nReplaces the bare \\\"Reports\\\" heading on the overview page with\\nPageHeader and PageHeaderContent, using the styleguide's new\\nReportsPictogram. The header runs full width under the navbar, with the\\nimplementation name above the title like other O3 apps, a white\\nbackground, a bottom border, and 16px of space before the action\\nbuttons.\\n\\nThe root container's 32px padding moves onto each page's content so\\nthe header can sit flush. The overview no longer passes the\\nbreadcrumb slot's negative top margin, which only offset that padding\\nand would otherwise pull the header under the navbar. The scheduled\\nreports and Reports Webview pages keep the same padding through a page\\nwrapper, so their layout doesn't change.\\n\\nReportsPictogram ships in a framework release after\\nopenmrs/openmrs-esm-core adds it, so this needs that release before it\\ntypechecks.\\n\\n* Mock the page header in the overview tests\\n\\nThe overview tests mock @openmrs/esm-framework with a factory that only\\nlists the exports they use. The overview now renders PageHeader,\\nPageHeaderContent and ReportsPictogram, so add simple mocks for them.\\n\\n* Assert that the Reports overview renders its page header\\n\\nThe overview test mocked PageHeader, PageHeaderContent and\\nReportsPictogram but never checked them, so it would still pass if the\\nheader or pictogram were removed. It now checks for the \\\"Reports\\\"\\nheading and the pictogram.\\n\\n* Drop the breadcrumbs slot from the Reports overview\\n\\nNothing renders into breadcrumbs-slot any more. No extension attaches to\\nit, and the app shell no longer mounts its breadcrumbs component. The\\noverview's slot had no class, so it rendered as an empty element and\\nremoving it doesn't change the layout. The test mock for ExtensionSlot\\ngoes with it.\\n\\n* Rename tests to drop the .component suffix\\n\\nTest files don't carry the component-kind suffix. Rename the three that\\ndid in admin-tools:\\n\\n- reports-app overview.component.test.tsx -> overview.test.tsx\\n- reports-app reports-data-overview.component.test.tsx -> reports-data-overview.test.tsx\\n- metadataexport-app view-package-action-button.component.test.tsx -> view-package-action-button.test.tsx\\n\\nThe only content change is the trailing newline Prettier adds to\\nreports-data-overview.test.tsx.\\n\\n* Remove breadcrumbs from the Reports app\\n\\nNothing renders into breadcrumbs-slot any more, so the Reports pages\\nwere rendering empty slots and registering breadcrumbs nobody reads.\\n\\n- Remove the breadcrumbs slot from the Scheduled reports and Reports\\n  data overview pages, and the .breadcrumb rule. Its negative top margin\\n  cancelled the page's top padding, so .page now drops its top padding\\n  instead and the content stays flush under the navbar.\\n- Remove the registerBreadcrumbs call from startupApp, along with the\\n  getFixedT setup that only it used.\\n- Drop the ExtensionSlot mock from the data overview test.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"feb0ba00e3382e0c55e4b3615648217d7d619198\",\"date\":\"2026-10-01T22:20:05+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Remove unused stylesheet classes from the reports app\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Delete 13 CSS Module classes in esm-reports-app that no component\\nreferences. Each stylesheet is a CSS Module, so a class only applies\\nwhen a file that imports that stylesheet uses it as styles.<name>, and\\nnone of these are:\\n\\n- root.scss: welcome, explainer (plus the @carbon/type import, which\\n  only welcome used)\\n- components/reports.scss: emptyButton, breadcrumbsSlot\\n- components/overlay.scss: closeButton, overlayContent (the desktop and\\n  tablet breakpoint blocks contained only overlayContent)\\n- components/run-report/run-report-form.scss: parameterElement,\\n  cancelActionButton, tableIcon, rowCellEven, rowCellOdd\\n- components/edit-scheduled-report/edit-scheduled-report-form.scss:\\n  reportButton\\n- components/simple-cron-editor/simple-cron-editor.scss: cronEditor\\n\\nrowCellEven, rowCellOdd and reportButton are still in use, but from\\nother stylesheets: the overview tables use the copies in reports.scss,\\nand the run report form uses the copy in run-report-form.scss. Only the\\nunreferenced duplicates are removed.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"fbda030326a3a0a691844ad052fe7aed34ca44ac\",\"date\":\"2026-10-01T21:08:13+03:00\",\"message\":\"chore: Remove inert Carbon CSS rules from reports app (#358)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"solomonfortune\",\"authorEmail\":\"solomonbuwule@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"a10120fa4fe525b60a32af2b713bccf0377bf2ad\",\"date\":\"2025-12-08T13:37:43+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Add ability to configure web preview url for reports (#190)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"CynthiaKamau\",\"authorEmail\":\"cynthiakamau54@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"29fe1166d3bf133130cb02f0da755d5fdef9fa64\",\"date\":\"2025-04-21T21:02:26+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Add a new ReportsDataOverviewComponent which directly renders raw report data (#67)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Emmanuel Nyachoke\",\"authorEmail\":\"achachiez@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"626b777d3894b352df757af94422b6f8a3852a19\",\"date\":\"2025-02-06T12:31:06+01:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-1494: Add report admin dashboard (#45)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* O3-1494: Added Report Admin pages\\n\\n- Reports overview\\n- Report schedules overview\\n\\n* O3-1494: Adjusted API calls to backend changes\\n\\n* O3-1494: Changes after code review\\n\\n* O3-1494: Changes after code review part2\\n\\n* O3-1494: Updated backend dependencies\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: druchniewicz <druchniewicz@soldevelo.com>\",\"authorName\":\"pwargulak\",\"authorEmail\":\"pwargulak@soldevelo.com\"}],\"totalCount\":7}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"18005517-9fe5-4943-8b94-df897eb41584","uuid":"9c6b3314-7ba9-4f8e-aff3-cb57cd306e44","timestamp":"2026-10-23T15:07:25.657Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"06a5b092b1cd90a40745932a80b20866ab0bec12\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T23:39:28+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Add page headers to the other Reports pa